// get -- one pixel of one sprite, and the row a blit reads.
//
// A pixel index is frame * w * h + row * w + col, flat: the loader walks its
// decoded rows in order and so does every blit, so nobody multiplies out a
// frame twice.
//
// d2_spr_px hands out the pixel list itself, which matters more than it looks.
// The blitters need it as a *parameter*, because a flat loop assigning into a
// list parameter runs at 4.3-5.0 Gpx/s while the same loop through lset runs at
// 1.0 (ARCHITECTURE.md section 3.1). Returning the list once per row is what
// buys that.
//
// d2_spr_put and d2_spr_at are the load-time and script-level accessors: they
// pay a call and a bounds check per pixel, which is the right trade for
// decoding art once and utterly the wrong one for drawing it every frame.

d2_spr_px(int p) {
  int[] px = (import asset_sprpx)[p];
} return int[] px;

d2_spr_put(int p, int i, int c) {
  int[] d2_spr_px_v = d2_spr_px(p);
  lset(d2_spr_px_v, i, c);
} return void;

d2_spr_at(int p, int i) {
  int[] px = d2_spr_px(p);
  int c = lget(px, i);
} return int c;
